8. Termination.

You may not convey a covered work except as expressly provided
under this License. Any attempt otherwise to convey a covered work
is void and will automatically terminate your rights under this
License (including any additional permissions granted under
clause 7). However, if you cease all violation of this License,
then your license from a particular copyright holder is reinstated
(a) provisionally, unless and until that copyright holder explicitly
and finally terminates your license, and (b) permanently, if that
copyright holder fails to notify you of the termination by some
reasonable means prior to 60 days after the cessation.

Moreover, your license from a particular copyright holder is
reinstated permanently if that copyright holder notifies you of the
termination by some reasonable means, you cease all violation of
this License, and you do not resume the violation within 60 days
after receiving the notice of the termination.

9. Acceptance Not Required for Having Copies.

You are not required to accept this License in order to receive or
run a copy of the Library. Ancillary propagation of a covered work
through settlement does not require acceptance. However, nothing
other than this License grants you the right to convey a covered
work. If you convey a covered work without accepting this License,
your license may be terminated under clause 8.

10. Automatic Licensing of Conveyed Works.

When you convey a covered work, the recipient automatically
receives a license from the original licensors to that work, subject
to the terms of this License. You are not obligated to enforce this
License on behalf of the original licensors.

11. Patents.

A "contributor" is a copyright holder who authorizes the use under
this License of a claim of a patent for which the contributor holds
the right to grant such authorization. Each contributor's claims
consist of the patent claims that the contributor has granted
authorization for. The "contributor's patent claims" are the patent
claims that the contributor has granted authorization for.

Each contributor grants you a non-exclusive, royalty-free license
under the contributor's patent claims to make, use, sell, offer for
sale, import and otherwise dispose of covered works involving the
contributor's patent claims. However, if you institute patent
litigation against any entity (including a cross-claim or counterclaim
in a lawsuit) alleging that a covered work infringes the contributor's
patent claims, your license from that contributor for the covered
work terminates on the date such litigation is instituted.

12. No Surrender of Others' Rights.

If conditions are imposed on you (whether by court order, agreement
or otherwise) that are inconsistent with the terms of this License,
you cannot comply with both those conditions and the terms of this
License. Consequently, you must not convey a covered work under the
conditions that are inconsistent with this License, even if those
conditions are imposed by a court order or by an agreement with a
third party.

